{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1301238-does-anything-majorly-bad-happen-if-you-just-ignore-training-times","id":1301238,"title":"Does anything majorly bad happen if you just ignore training times","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-03-31T00:28:06-07:00","id":1301238,"title":"Does anything majorly bad happen if you just ignore training times","content":"Apologies if this has been debated to death already, but as the title says.<br /> <br /> I'll do anything for an easy life and on our third game into the campaign, training times at first glance just seem like unnecessary additional book-keeping that none of us can be bothered with. Your thoughts please, will our hubris lead to our untimely demise or do you ignore them too and allow characters to insta-level?<br /> <br /> Edit to add: we'd be spending XP between sessions obviously, not in-game. We're not complete monsters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229925-hello-i-did-up-a-scavenger-lands-map-based-on-3e\" target=\"_blank\">3e Scavenger Lands map</a><br /> <a href=\"https://imgur.com/a/NQewCv0\" target=\"_blank\">3e Combat tracker card</a><br /> <a href=\"https://imgur.com/uGrZk2r\" target=\"_blank\">2e Nexus map</a>","edited":{"userid":1079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1079-megapope","user":"Megapope","date":". 03-31-2019, 03:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1079-megapope","name":"Megapope","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T01:01:09-07:00","id":1301243,"title":"","content":"The biggest issue that comes to my mind is just that players will occasionally end up with things you hadn't planned for them to have. Now obviously it won't be as problematic as them just being able to buy new powers in the middle of a fight, but it might still trip you up from time to time. <br /> <br /> On a more narrative aspect training has a few ways to be used that I find somewhat beneficial. Like on the low end being able to describe how a character trains can work nicely for character traits, then there's the tradition of enemies or what have you just interrupting training. Then there's the perk of making that part of downtime easier to plan since characters are off studying or working out or whatever they need to do while waiting for reinforcements to arrive so the circle can focus on bashing in Tain Without Reflections skull and not getting swarmed by however many undead a magnitude 5 group is. <br /> <br /> There's also my personal standing that it kind of takes something away from the favored/ unfavored divide if you remove training time since the xp gap isn't that big. (10 unfavored charm 8 favored, current ability x2 for unfavored, favored is [current x2]-1) So it feels like that becomes more meaningless if characters master it all with equal rapidity. I don't know just feels like there's something to be said that with a solar starting with a dot in sail it takes about 3.5 months for one who isn't favoring become one of the best sailors humanly possible (Going to 5 dots.) vs the 2 weeks it takes the one who favored it to get the same results.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T02:11:14-07:00","id":1301251,"title":"","content":"We've tried to use them multiple times and always ended up dropping them. They're an enormous hassle.<br /> <br /> They also severely dissuade people from buying attributes, because the training times are so long. <br /> <br /> One game I play is so action packed/has such a split party that most sessions are 1-2 days. If we used training times, some PCs would have scores of XP unspent.<br /> <br /> We do demand some justification though. You can't just one day learn Snake 5. You need a teacher or scroll, and then buy 1 dot a session while you practice in your free time and use it in fights. Etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T02:58:38-07:00","id":1301256,"title":"","content":"My first EX3 game dropped training times in favour of having specific points where we could spend experience points (and make rolls for sorcerous workings and the like). It was mostly a side effect of the insane pace of the game, but there weren't really any issues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T03:10:13-07:00","id":1301259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Megapope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1301238-does-anything-majorly-bad-happen-if-you-just-ignore-training-times#post1301238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll do anything for an easy life and on our third game into the campaign, training times at first glance just seem like unnecessary additional book-keeping that none of us can be bothered with. Your thoughts please, will our hubris lead to our untimely demise or do you ignore them too and allow characters to insta-level?<br /> <br /> Edit to add: we'd be spending XP between sessions obviously, not in-game. We're not complete monsters.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Nothing will break, but my experience is that having to spend XP in bursts of downtime rather than drip-feeding it as soon as it becomes available is better for pacing and makes for a more satisfying power curve. It also forces players to make some interesting choices in what to train, rather than dogmatically sticking to a pre-determined advancement path they wrote up at the campaign's start.<br /> <br /> (Also, I just inherently enjoy fiddling with it.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T03:16:31-07:00","id":1301261,"title":"","content":"I'll be honest, I find the drip-feeding better because people have 2 sessions to learn each charm.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, having it in groups probably leads to better characters as their charms work together more.<br /> <br /> On the other other hand, it's kind of fun the way PCs have random charms that they bought to deal with a particular issue at a particular time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T04:22:24-07:00","id":1301268,"title":"","content":"It doesn't break anything, but it still gives me the same irritation as I get during a movie or TV show when a character magically <i>has</i> a skill or attribute without so much as a hint of it prior to that (never seeing a master fighter spar or even exercise, not seeing a supposed genius crack a book, and so on).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T04:57:02-07:00","id":1301271,"title":"","content":"My compromise is that I allow one Long Term training goal (this is usually a Stat or something that is going to take months) and one Short Term training goal (ability, charm etc). That way, they don't have to block themselves off from nice things while they are working on their cardio.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T05:04:34-07:00","id":1301272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1301238-does-anything-majorly-bad-happen-if-you-just-ignore-training-times?p=1301251#post1301251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We've tried to use them multiple times and always ended up dropping them. They're an enormous hassle.<br /> <br /> They also severely dissuade people from buying attributes, because the training times are so long.<br /> <br /> One game I play is so action packed/has such a split party that most sessions are 1-2 days. If we used training times, some PCs would have scores of XP unspent.<br /> <br /> We do demand some justification though. You can't just one day learn Snake 5. You need a teacher or scroll, and then buy 1 dot a session while you practice in your free time and use it in fights. Etc.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Same. My games are usually very &quot;daily&quot;, that\u00b4s it, most sessions are one or two days, with very little downtime because player characters are very busy. So, if I applied training times, we would have the problem of players having 40-50 XP, and not enough time to train to spend their XP!<br /> <br /> So, I demand justification. You want to learn sorcery/occult/martial arts? Find a mentor, a secret manual, or whatever. And it doesn\u00b4t matter how much experience you have, you can only improve the same trait one dot at a time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13031-clophiroth","name":"Clophiroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13031_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T05:13:35-07:00","id":1301274,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that sounds the same as us. If your character tried to pick a lock and disguise themselves that session, you can buy one dot of Larceny. You can't buy two dots, and you can't buy Sail.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T05:20:02-07:00","id":1301277,"title":"","content":"I use the training times, but typically my games have 3-5 sessions before a travel burst (or 8-10 sessions, and then 3 months in game of down time), so it works for my pacing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T05:46:43-07:00","id":1301282,"title":"","content":"Generally my group doesn't use training times, but the work around that we use is the story itself. All xp spent must relate to something that the character did during the story. Any points spent that are not traceable to the story require a short story describing how the character acquired the new skills.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T07:13:01-07:00","id":1301301,"title":"","content":"You could just treat training times as &quot;how long has it been since I last bought this trait?&quot; and let them take anything that they can reasonably argue they've been working on. That way it just becomes an incentive to broaden skills.<br /> <br /> You can ignore them completely if the characters actually train.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T09:50:28-07:00","id":1301331,"title":"","content":"I will also remind that the section on training times in the core (pg 178 since I always lose it myself.) does also say that it isn't like characters need to exclusively be doing the training. Also that practical experience can count for training. So hey you remember how the ship you were on got attacked by Lintha and you said you'd help out around the ship while the wounded crew recovered, great you can buy those new sailing dots; needed to act as the tough while the party face negotiated prices and contracts recently, great you've managed to hone your ability to project your presence and can buy those new dots or reveal that you were actually paying more attention than thought and buy up some bureaucracy dots; almost murdered by a Wyld Hunt, well you're definitely motivated to improve on whatever means you used to survive it during the escape. And through it all you've been spending essence in stressful situations, so now you've spent the evening fine tuning it to make sure you got your new power down pat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T10:27:25-07:00","id":1301341,"title":"","content":"Nothing breaks, though as people have said it's good to have some sort of alternative around that's less bookkeeping but still useful for pacing things out a bit.<br /> <br /> I always felt the WoD had it better here: You can't raise a trait with XP more than once a Story, and it needs in-game justification. This does plenty to avoid &quot;I learned Crane Style overnight,&quot; but it scales to the pace of the game more readily than training times based on in-game time rather than out-of-game time units.<br /> <br /> If you want to highlight favored vs. non-favored, have favored limited by Session, and non-favored by Story.<br /> <br /> This is means dealing with any Charms the modify training times easier to adapt rather than figuring out what to do with them if you flat our remove any mechanical training limits besides having XP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T10:42:57-07:00","id":1301343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1301238-does-anything-majorly-bad-happen-if-you-just-ignore-training-times?p=1301341#post1301341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always felt the WoD had it better here: You can't raise a trait with XP more than once a Story, and it needs in-game justification. This does plenty to avoid &quot;I learned Crane Style overnight,&quot; but it scales to the pace of the game more readily than training times based on in-game time rather than out-of-game time units.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh, that's not bad.<br /> <br /> Still more hassle than I can be bothered with, and I wouldn't want to stop training montages, but I can see the value.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T10:51:16-07:00","id":1301346,"title":"","content":"our group has mostly intact training times, but since we're a pretty high-paced game we've been granting 1 instant charm purchase at the end of each session where a character has earned a level-two stunt. Before we instituted this, we had a pretty big xp pileup","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T11:00:25-07:00","id":1301351,"title":"","content":"I've considered it at times - but the thing is, players can accrue XP at a rate that doesn't at all match the normal chronological progression of the game itself.<br /> <br /> What I mean is, if a game is focusing on a dungeon crawl through an ancient ruined manse, with lots of work required to get there, and whatnot - and if your players are earning 4xp per session - then even before that crawl is done... your players might suddenly have a buttload of XP.<br /> <br /> As ST, you build your encounters and stories to the power and ability level of your players. If they can - at the drop of a hat, say that they're blowing 24 xp to learn a bunch of new charms that completely change the power dynamics of what they can do, then you can quickly find yourself utterly boned because your players are now suddenly blazing through stuff that was meant to be great challenges.<br /> <br /> equally, I like the time-gating mechanism of it, because it makes the investments more meaningful for the players. If they're on a grand adventure, then taking three weeks out of busy schedule to gain a dot of some skill or ability suddenly seems... very expensive. A good ST will even remind the players that the game world around them continues on while they're training. That army you're trying to prevent getting to that manse you're protecting? It'll still be marching while you're training. That people you're trying to save from starvation while you're learning a charm that will end their hunger, they'll still be starving while you're learning it.<br /> <br /> heck, in the game I'm currently ST'ing my players have more than enough XP to get up to essence 4 - but there's so much stuff going on, that they don't feel they have time to sit down and level that up - because they know that the world might end. I like that the game allows for that.<br /> <br /> <br /> Heck, I've actually considered experimenting with games the other way around: No xp, but only training time. Of course, things like WP, virtues... that's going to be tricky to balance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T12:33:34-07:00","id":1301375,"title":"","content":"The problem with the &quot;train and deal with in-game consequences, or try to solve it with what you have,&quot; is that it gets old quick. It's one thing to use it as spice here and there. It's a different thing for the system to constantly be hanging it over the characters' heads.<br /> <br /> If I want the players to feel their characters have had some time to rest up, do some training, and prepare for a big plot that they're about to engage in.... I don't want to have to throw in a three month downtime just to be fair to everyone on their character focus training times. If you use the RAW, a character focusing on native and MA Charms is normally going to be able to spend most of their XP, while Evocation and Sorcery focused characters are going to start lagging behind because those have longer training times... because reasons.<br /> <br /> Tying advancement to narrative time instead of in-game time still lets you force time choices, it just doesn't have to abide by the arbitrary math of the training times chart. You generally just have to adjust from, &quot;do I train at all?&quot; to, &quot;which training do I do?&quot; If you know you can only buy a new spell once every 3-5 sessions, and there are two spells you don't have yet that seem like obvious ones you're going to want in the next two sessions... boom dilemma achieved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T14:04:51-07:00","id":1301399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1301238-does-anything-majorly-bad-happen-if-you-just-ignore-training-times?p=1301375#post1301375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with the &quot;train and deal with in-game consequences, or try to solve it with what you have,&quot; is that it gets old quick. It's one thing to use it as spice here and there. It's a different thing for the system to constantly be hanging it over the characters' heads.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is my experience. It seems like a good idea, starts out good, but gets pretty irritating and awkward.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T16:39:20-07:00","id":1301458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1301238-does-anything-majorly-bad-happen-if-you-just-ignore-training-times?p=1301301#post1301301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could just treat training times as &amp;quot;how long has it been since I last bought this trait?&amp;quot; and let them take anything that they can reasonably argue they've been working on. That way it just becomes an incentive to broaden skills.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is 100% how it\u2019s supposed to work: the listed times are explicitly for if training <i>isn\u2019t</i> the only thing you\u2019re doing all day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T16:46:04-07:00","id":1301462,"title":"","content":"Not... entirely.<br /> <br /> The training times assume you're actively training in a narrative way. You aren't only training, and you aren't only training one trait, but you have to actually be training. You don't get to learn a new Terrestrial Circle spell two weeks after you learned your last spell... unless you started studying it right away. Finding the resources to learn the new spell two weeks after you learned your last spell, means another two weeks until you get the new one.<br /> <br /> If you want to buy a Melee specialty in swords, the timer starts when you start working specifically on swords in game, not since your last specialty purchase.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T02:25:53-07:00","id":1301556,"title":"","content":"Yeah, my hack is more &quot;automatically assume that the character <i>has</i> been training to a sufficient degree since their last purchase unless it's really obvious they haven't&quot;<br /> <br /> Also if you specifically have a training montage just let them buy whatever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T04:53:10-07:00","id":1301580,"title":"","content":"I can see it having an undesirable negative impact on players who have issues with paranoia, not the Jon Chung paranoia combo kind, I mean the sort that stems from anxiety disorders etc &quot;if I personally don't have enough xp to adapt my way out of the situation then people will be mad at me&quot;. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T05:58:43-07:00","id":1301592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1301238-does-anything-majorly-bad-happen-if-you-just-ignore-training-times?p=1301580#post1301580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">adapt my way out of the situation</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, yeah, that brings to mind another potential reason <i>I'm</i> not particularly be fond of the idea of axing training times - annoyance at folks treating the XP system as special Amazo-style adaptation power for PCs. If I run a game where your bookish Eclipse gets imprisoned, it's probably gonna raise my hackles a bit if she starts buying Athletics Charms out of nowhere so she can snap her manacles off and Mountain-Crossing Leap to freedom before I even send a Dynast in to question her and come away from it questioning his own beliefs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T06:43:10-07:00","id":1301607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1301238-does-anything-majorly-bad-happen-if-you-just-ignore-training-times?p=1301592#post1301592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, yeah, that brings to mind another potential reason <i>I'm</i> not particularly be fond of the idea of axing training times - annoyance at folks treating the XP system as special Amazo-style adaptation power for PCs. If I run a game where your bookish Eclipse gets imprisoned, it's probably gonna raise my hackles a bit if she starts buying Athletics Charms out of nowhere so she can snap her manacles off and Mountain-Crossing Leap to freedom before I even send a Dynast in to question her and come away from it questioning his own beliefs.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about an extended training montage, ala Iroh in Avatar before she breaks out?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T08:04:25-07:00","id":1301627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1301238-does-anything-majorly-bad-happen-if-you-just-ignore-training-times?p=1301607#post1301607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about an extended training montage, ala Iroh in Avatar before she breaks out?</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a hard montage to dismiss, but I think the issue there is Iroh was out of commission and action in the story while that training took place, where as we prolly don't want our bookish Twilight to spent X sessions describing a training montage while the characters are out doing what Solar do.<br /> <br /> In any case, that's what training times are supposed to do, yeh; increase verisimilitude (ugh, there's a 2e bugaboo if I evrr wrote one) by calling out that people are, to a certain degree, what they can do. When people can do cool new things, that's a pretty major shift to the character that should get some attention.<br /> <br /> We use training times in my game, but I keep finding reasons to fiat around them (prev incarnation mentors, hyperbolic time chambers with the serial #'s filed off) because my game is taking place at an emergency pace, but a given session is likely only going to be one or two battles or three to five social scenes.<br /> <br /> Dunno, it's a tough nut to crack","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron-crowns.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron...dianportal.com</a> Visit Golden Shackles, Iron Crowns; a 3rd Edition Exalted Campaign ongoing since 2014","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","name":"Janissary87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2711_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T09:33:17-07:00","id":1301656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1301238-does-anything-majorly-bad-happen-if-you-just-ignore-training-times?p=1301607#post1301607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about an extended training montage, ala Iroh in Avatar before she breaks out?</div> </div> </div> </div>Does that in any way describe what I was saying?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T11:24:16-07:00","id":1301700,"title":"","content":"How many book-ish Essence 3 Solars are sitting on up to 63 XP to suddenly get to Athletics 5 and buy up to four non-favored Charms? And for some reason are neglecting have Larceny, Presence, and Socialize as potential ways out of imprisonment. I mean... Seasoned Criminal Method and Spurious Presence basically make getting a guard's uniform and just walking out of the prison breeze, and would take 23 XP max. Plus as an Essence 3 Eclipse who knows what else they have already to make this all easier even if they've avoided learning about criminal behavior until now?<br /> <br /> IME... a 40 XP gap is more then enough incentive to stick to using your brains to break out, rather than trying to suddenly go from zero to amazing on brawn instead.<br /> <br /> And if you're hoping to keep a character imprisoned before they escape, you need to fiat how long the Dynast takes to get there anyway. The Larceny method above takes an Eclipse a max of three days to learn, compared to the 15 weeks to train from Athletics 0 to 5. So if you want to make sure they don't slip away, you have to have the serious threat interrogator coming at the speed of narrative fast as it is.<br /> <br /> What do training times really do? XP costs and training times both provide the same incentives: if you need to do something ASAP find a way with the stuff your character is mechanically favored to work with. So we don't really need them for that.<br /> <br /> If you want a plot point to happen, so you cut off all the ways a character could avoid it by putting them behind Charms in Abilities they don't work with (yet) so they can't train in those fast enough... you're already using your ST fiat to make it happen, and I assure you, you still can easily enough if you want to; after all you already made a prison that takes an Athletics 5, Essence 3 Solar Charm to bust out of, you can keep finding holes in the Charms and ensure the prison exploits them if you really want to.<br /> <br /> And this still ignores that axing training times doesn't mean a free for all of &quot;if you have the XP, you can have it,&quot; without any other considerations .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T15:26:38-07:00","id":1301734,"title":"","content":"Yeah, even without training times, I just wouldn't let someone buy 5 dots of an ability at the end of a session.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T16:49:48-07:00","id":1301746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1301238-does-anything-majorly-bad-happen-if-you-just-ignore-training-times?p=1301592#post1301592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, yeah, that brings to mind another potential reason <i>I'm</i> not particularly be fond of the idea of axing training times - annoyance at folks treating the XP system as special Amazo-style adaptation power for PCs. If I run a game where your bookish Eclipse gets imprisoned, it's probably gonna raise my hackles a bit if she starts buying Athletics Charms out of nowhere so she can snap her manacles off and Mountain-Crossing Leap to freedom before I even send a Dynast in to question her and come away from it questioning his own beliefs.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I honestly couldn't imagine any of my players A) sitting on that much XP and B) even doing that because C) it's daft","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229925-hello-i-did-up-a-scavenger-lands-map-based-on-3e\" target=\"_blank\">3e Scavenger Lands map</a><br /> <a href=\"https://imgur.com/a/NQewCv0\" target=\"_blank\">3e Combat tracker card</a><br /> <a href=\"https://imgur.com/uGrZk2r\" target=\"_blank\">2e Nexus map</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1079-megapope","name":"Megapope","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T17:18:42-07:00","id":1301760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Janissary87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1301238-does-anything-majorly-bad-happen-if-you-just-ignore-training-times?p=1301627#post1301627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is a hard montage to dismiss, but I think the issue there is Iroh was out of commission and action in the story while that training took place, where as we prolly don't want our bookish Twilight to spent X sessions describing a training montage while the characters are out doing what Solar do.</div> </div> </div> </div>How I'd handle it depends on why she's been captured. Normally when a PC gets captured* its because they did something really dumb and its less disruptive than killing them and working in their replacement.<br /> <br /> *I strongly recommend asking if this is okay, its uncommon but players rarely tend to tell roleplay groups about times they were held against their will. You're more likely to encounter are players who had their PCs captured by GMs who used the situation as an execuse to get their sick fuck on.<br /> <br /> Even when the GM isn't a certified creep this is a major place where sexism tends to really creep into roleplay. A male captive tends to be subject to things that show he's a badass if he's a slave he's a gladiator or performing backbreaking physical labour, if he's been taken by the enemy they'll invariably try and break him through pain. A female captive in the same situation is much more likely to suffer an assault on her dignity and threats of violation often in the name of realism.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T06:31:50-07:00","id":1301886,"title":"","content":"It's not uncommon for me to run sessions which involve multiple back-to-back days. And it's not fun for me to tell a player, &quot;Sorry but you'll have to wait until next month, when we finally wrap up this current arc, before you can spend experience.&quot; So I just allow players to spend exp at the end of any session, or at the beginning of a session, as long as they notify me what they're spending it on. The only exception is Charms and Sorcery which I ask that they notify me they're buying at the end of a session so I have plenty of time to look at it between games and get a feel for how it works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T08:02:51-07:00","id":1301909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Megapope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1301238-does-anything-majorly-bad-happen-if-you-just-ignore-training-times?p=1301746#post1301746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I honestly couldn't imagine any of my players A) sitting on that much XP and B) even doing that because C) it's daft</div> </div> </div> </div>So A) clearly you've never played with someone who isn't a fully committed gamer. My wife just doesn't have that much time to look up charms and between sessions she kinda forgets about the game so she doesn't have a clear idea of what to spend xp on when she's got it. B) Apparently you've never played with an exploitive player either because C) that's absolutely what some people would do given the chance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T08:10:39-07:00","id":1301912,"title":"","content":"In my experience, some people sit on their experience because they're not sure what to get, but those tend to be the people who are not the sort to buy stuff to get them out of a certain situation.<br /> <br /> Of course, people do buy charms at the end of sessions that they think will be useful for the next session, but I don't really mind that. For one thing, if it's too situational, it'll help them for one session, and then not again for ages.<br /> <br /> (There's also a theory of learning that this is kind of how things work, hence all that Task-Based Learning that was fashionable 10 years ago, but it's a bit complex.)<br /> <br /> Anyway, obviously sitting in a jail cell and learning Larceny 5 and a charm for escaping is ridiculous, and I just wouldn't let people do it. But I don't think making people spend 4 months weight-lifting to buy a dot of Strength, as realistic as it might be, is actually very practical for a game. There's other ways to do it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T11:58:39-07:00","id":1301966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1301238-does-anything-majorly-bad-happen-if-you-just-ignore-training-times?p=1301909#post1301909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So A) clearly you've never played with someone who isn't a fully committed gamer. My wife just doesn't have that much time to look up charms and between sessions she kinda forgets about the game so she doesn't have a clear idea of what to spend xp on when she's got it. B) Apparently you've never played with an exploitive player either because C) that's absolutely what some people would do given the chance.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're absolutely right, none of my players are like that! Ten points to the house of your choice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229925-hello-i-did-up-a-scavenger-lands-map-based-on-3e\" target=\"_blank\">3e Scavenger Lands map</a><br /> <a href=\"https://imgur.com/a/NQewCv0\" target=\"_blank\">3e Combat tracker card</a><br /> <a href=\"https://imgur.com/uGrZk2r\" target=\"_blank\">2e Nexus map</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1079-megapope","name":"Megapope","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T12:01:50-07:00","id":1301967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1301238-does-anything-majorly-bad-happen-if-you-just-ignore-training-times?p=1301886#post1301886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not uncommon for me to run sessions which involve multiple back-to-back days. And it's not fun for me to tell a player, &amp;quot;Sorry but you'll have to wait until next month, when we finally wrap up this current arc, before you can spend experience.&amp;quot; So I just allow players to spend exp at the end of any session, or at the beginning of a session, as long as they notify me what they're spending it on. The only exception is Charms and Sorcery which I ask that they notify me they're buying at the end of a session so I have plenty of time to look at it between games and get a feel for how it works.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is pretty much our agreed upon system. I trust my players and we've all been gaming together for close to 20 years so we communicate well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229925-hello-i-did-up-a-scavenger-lands-map-based-on-3e\" target=\"_blank\">3e Scavenger Lands map</a><br /> <a href=\"https://imgur.com/a/NQewCv0\" target=\"_blank\">3e Combat tracker card</a><br /> <a href=\"https://imgur.com/uGrZk2r\" target=\"_blank\">2e Nexus map</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1079-megapope","name":"Megapope","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T13:10:23-07:00","id":1301988,"title":"","content":"I have literally always just assumed that my players were the training of screen leading up to when they purchased the abilities, and that the abilities were payoffs. Plus my campaigns tend to use 'soft time' to begin with because I don't know how long things take.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23919-nabirius","name":"Nabirius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T08:13:20-07:00","id":1302216,"title":"","content":"I see (and treat) training times as a safety valve for helping players focus on the long-term arc of their character's development instead of whatever they happen to be doing right now. Saying that once you decide you want something it will be X time before you get it helps.<br /> <br /> That said, I've never felt the need to be super strict about them. The layer of unreality between calendar time and narrative time makes it really awkward. So in practice I end up holding advancement to in-between story beats rather than specific amounts of downtime. If the players fight someone in Chiaroscuro and then immediately chase him across the desert for two straight uneventful weeks before picking up the fight again in a hidden manse, I wouldn't count that as a story break. But on the flip side, if they were to liberate Thorns from the Mask of Winters and the head of Oct breaks through from Autochthonia in the middle of town while they're still pulling Volcano Cutter out of the smoldering remains of Juggernaut, they'll still get a chance to spend their XP before we resume play. In short I'm not going to incentivize or penalize advancement mechanics with timing choices made for dramatic effect. But as a general principle I expect that where the XP goes when the break does happen will be mostly a formality because the player already indicated where it was probably going to go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":456,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","user":"Blackwell","date":". 04-04-2019, 10:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-07T14:55:50-07:00","id":1303411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Clophiroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1301238-does-anything-majorly-bad-happen-if-you-just-ignore-training-times?p=1301272#post1301272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Same. My games are usually very &quot;daily&quot;, that\u00b4s it, most sessions are one or two days, with very little downtime because player characters are very busy. So, if I applied training times, we would have the problem of players having 40-50 XP, and not enough time to train to spend their XP!<br /> <br /> So, I demand justification. You want to learn sorcery/occult/martial arts? Find a mentor, a secret manual, or whatever. And it doesn\u00b4t matter how much experience you have, you can only improve the same trait one dot at a time.</div> </div> </div> </div>We have found the same thing occurs. Keeping training times but helping players feel it isn't so onerous I've instituted training accelerators as suggested in the book.<br /> Want to speed up learning? Then trainers knock it down one time increment from the core training times. e.g. Months to weeks, weeks, to days, days-halved. Find an exceptional trainer and times are knocked down two increments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/977-major","name":"Major","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar977_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-07T15:50:25-07:00","id":1303421,"title":"","content":"I lays think of <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qCH5kJqCm-Q\" target=\"_blank\">this scene</a> when when I consider spending xp in the middle of a session.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I want to play <a href=\"https://forum.atlas-games.com/t/adelbert-a-magi-of-hermes-look-at-intellego-and-astrology/8146/382\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> as a starting character, I don't even care what game.","edited":{"userid":872,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/872-apromor","user":"Apromor","date":". 04-08-2019, 10:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/872-apromor","name":"Apromor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar872_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-07T21:55:38-07:00","id":1303475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Major</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1301238-does-anything-majorly-bad-happen-if-you-just-ignore-training-times?p=1303411#post1303411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We have found the same thing occurs. Keeping training times but helping players feel it isn't so onerous I've instituted training accelerators as suggested in the book.<br /> Want to speed up learning? Then trainers knock it down one time increment from the core training times. e.g. Months to weeks, weeks, to days, days-halved. Find an exceptional trainer and times are knocked down two increments.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Find a legendary trainer, and the training time is knocked down to a musical montage!<br /> <br /> Jokes aside, we used the same system in our Mage campaign.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13031-clophiroth","name":"Clophiroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13031_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-08T01:13:27-07:00","id":1303487,"title":"","content":"In our current solo game I spend xp whenever, usually in response to new threats.<br /> <br /> That said it\u2019s A a solo game and B a casteless lunar game so it\u2019s kinda appropriate.<br /> <br /> Side note: thanks for making casteless worth playing, 3e devs!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","name":"Maseiken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1247_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-09T07:01:16-07:00","id":1303770,"title":"","content":"I'm in two games right now, one of which has waived training times entirely (I run this one) and one has loosened them. In the game without training times it has not caused any problems, and in fact allowed the party to occasionally find a solution that they would otherwise have had issues with. Just this last session several of them bought up stealth dots/charms or larceny &quot;I'm totally supposed to be here&quot; charms in preparation for an infiltration scene. If this hadn't happened then more of the party would have had to sit on the sidelines of that session because the players really wanted to be sneaky. In the game I'm playing in that has training times, we have loosened them, and if we hadn't it would be a rather large issue. Although that may be due to the atypical pacing of the game (roughly 2 sessions per in-game day so far).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9124-satoshi","name":"satoshi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-10T07:53:43-07:00","id":1303943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Megapope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1301238-does-anything-majorly-bad-happen-if-you-just-ignore-training-times#post1301238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apologies if this has been debated to death already, but as the title says.<br /> <br /> I'll do anything for an easy life and on our third game into the campaign, training times at first glance just seem like unnecessary additional book-keeping that none of us can be bothered with. Your thoughts please, will our hubris lead to our untimely demise or do you ignore them too and allow characters to insta-level?<br /> <br /> Edit to add: we'd be spending XP between sessions obviously, not in-game. We're not complete monsters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing major, but expect new charms to pop up between sessions of what'd otherwise be rushed for the characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-10T08:31:30-07:00","id":1303953,"title":"","content":"As far as I'm concerned, having characters get a new charm every 2 sessions is... well, basically fine. I don't see an issue with it.<br /> <br /> If you don't like it, then yeah, training times.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-10T08:52:15-07:00","id":1303957,"title":"","content":"Realistically, unless you're running a story were multiple sessions are necessary to resolve a single day's activities, you're going to see Charms every few sessions anyway.<br /> <br /> Though to repeat myself from earlier, there is a functional alternative in 'narrative' pacing where how often you can raise traits is measured in things like sessions, or stories, rather than days and weeks, so you have some additional control of the pace of advancement, but aren't fighting the pace of your story in the process.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}